  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is the dominant signal (rna_only 0.52 vs image_only 0.23), and multiprofile+avgpool lifts RNA from 0.52→0.65. However, we have only tested one RNA encoder (scvi_n200) across all five experiments, leaving the most fundamental representation choice unexplored. Question: config_036 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_002 (same but scvi_n200), isolating whether the scgpt pre-trained gene-expression representation outperforms the scvi latent embedding. Why this is the best next experiment: RNA encoder quality is the highest-leverage design decision because it determines the primary signal in every multimodal configuration. If scgpt substantially outperforms scvi_n200, the entire multimodal search direction shifts; if it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 and can confidently build on it. This reduces uncertainty on the most important axis before committing further budget to aggregation or fusion variations on top of a potentially suboptimal RNA representation."
}

